oic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.13113515515986,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":77.0,"_gate_pool_share":0.24714051042121965,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.03499650956978562,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":7.5,"_gate_margins":0.00135518114795235,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":51.4,"_gate_fund_growth":0.07796435271150377,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":78.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.1627485864707161,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.010584809656945237,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":82.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.52082,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Amneal Pharmaceuticals, Inc., a global biopharmaceutical company, develops, manufactures, markets, and distributes generics, injectables, biosimilars, and specialty branded pharmaceutical products in the United States, India, Ireland, and internationally. The company operates through three segments: Affordable Medicines, Specialty, and AvKARE. The Affordable Medicines segment offers dosage forms and delivery systems, which include immediate and extended-release oral solids, powders, liquids, sterile injectables, nasal sprays, inhalation and respiratory products, biosimilar products, ophthalmics, films, transdermal patches, and topicals. The Specialty segment develops, promotes, sells, and distributes pharmaceutical products with a focus on central nervous system and endocrine disorders, including Parkinson's disease. This segment provides Rytary, an oral capsule formulation of carbidopa-levodopa to treat Parkinson's disease, post-encephalitic parkinsonism, and parkinsonism; Unithroid and ONGENTYS for the treatment of hypothyroidism; and CREXONT, which is use for the treatment of Parkinson's disease. The AvKARE segment offers pharmaceuticals, medical and surgical products, and services primarily to governmental agencies, the Department of Defense, and the Department of Veterans Affairs. This segment also distributes bottle and unit dose pharmaceuticals under the AvKARE and AvPAK names; and packages and distributes pharmaceuticals and vitamins to its retail and institutional customers. It sells its products through wholesalers, distributors, retail pharmacies, managed care organizations, purchasing co-ops, hospitals, government agencies, institutions, and pharmaceutical companies. The company was formerly known as Atlas Holdings, Inc. and changed its name to Amneal Pharmaceuticals, Inc. in 2018. Amneal Pharmaceuticals, Inc. was founded in 2002 and is headquartered in Bridgewater, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Chirag K. Patel | Co-Founder, Co-CEO, President & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $347K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $31K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Amneal Pharmaceuticals, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $7.6B market cap on $3.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +2.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 36%.","The business throws off $270M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.72\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 52% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.533026113671276},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $7.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-7667124.49},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Healthcare peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 13% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Financial quality scores above most Healthcare peers","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Liquidity Mapping Around (AMRX) Price Events","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/78/Liquidity_Mapping_Around_AMRX_Price_Events_112626105601_1795751761.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795751761.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (AMRX) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/20/Price-Driven_Insight_from_AMRX_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_111726020801_1794899281.html","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794899281.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Amneal to Participate in Piper Sandler 38th Annual Healthcare Conference","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/amneal-participate-piper-sandler-38th-210500595.html","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795467900.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Novo's Sogroya Gets FDA Label Expansion for Pediatric Turner Syndrome","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3034030/novo-s-sogroya-gets-fda-label-expansion-for-pediatric-turner-syndrome?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Ccompany_news_medical_sector-3034030","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795449960.0,"origin"